flowchart TD
  Start["New repo, nothing set up yet -- goal: prompts arrive with the right files already attached"]

  subgraph Once["Step 1 -- one-time, per repo (minutes)"]
    direction TB
    Doctor["uv run hybrid-retrieval doctor -- checks python, tree-sitter grammars, sqlite FTS5, sqlite-vec, whether the dense extra is installed"]
    Scan["uv run hybrid-retrieval scan /path/repo -- dry run: lists what WOULD be indexed (index/walker.py discover), respects .gitignore. Use it to catch a repo that is 90% vendored files before paying for an index"]
    Index["uv run hybrid-retrieval index /path/repo -- the only mandatory step. Chunks every file with its language adapter (lang/*.py), writes FTS5 rows + the import graph (index/edges.py) into REPO/.retrieval/index.db. Seconds, CPU only"]
    Gitignore["Add .retrieval/ to .gitignore -- scripts/add_gitignore.py does it. The index lives inside the repo (decision 11), it is not meant to be committed"]
    Doctor --> Scan --> Index --> Gitignore
  end

  Start --> Doctor

  subgraph Optional["Step 2 -- optional quality layers, skip both and BM25 alone still works"]
    direction TB
    Embed["uv run hybrid-retrieval embed /path/repo -- dense vectors for meaning-match ('retry backoff' finds a file that never says 'retry'). Slow, GPU-bound, needs --extra dense. The daemon also backfills these in the background (embed/backfill.py)"]
    TrainGit["uv run hybrid-retrieval train /path/repo -- mines git history (gitlog.py): commit message = the prompt, files touched = the right answer. Trains a LightGBM ranker to REPO/.retrieval/ranker.txt. Needs real history, a fresh repo has nothing to learn from"]
    TrainSess["uv run hybrid-retrieval train-sessions -- same idea from agent transcripts instead of commits (--target touched|edited). Better signal than git when you have session history"]
    Embed --> TrainGit --> TrainSess
  end

  Gitignore --> Embed
  Gitignore -->|"skip the extras"| Serve

  subgraph Wire["Step 3 -- wire it into Claude Code"]
    direction TB
    Serve["uv run hybrid-retrieval serve -- one resident daemon serving ALL repos. The hook autostarts it, so running it by hand is only for watching logs"]
    Hook["Add the UserPromptSubmit hook to .claude/settings.json -- a hooks entry of type command running: python3 /ABS/PATH/hook/shim.py"]
    Py3["Always invoke via python3, never the executable bit -- a hook that cannot exec fails silently and looks identical to a hook that chose to skip"]
    Serve --> Hook --> Py3
  end

  TrainSess --> Serve

  subgraph Live["Step 4 -- what happens on every prompt after that (see refactor/pipeline-architecture.mmd for the internals)"]
    direction TB
    Skip{"retrieve/skip.py should_skip -- prompt under 8 chars, under 2 usable terms, or matches a skip pattern?"}
    Nothing["Inject nothing. Most cheap prompts should land here; injecting on 'yes' is pure token waste"]
    Pipe["retrieve/pipeline.py retrieve(): BM25 + dense -> RRF fuse -> LightGBM rerank -> confidence gate -> top_n (default 5)"]
    Inject["Hook renders <retrieved-context> and Claude Code prepends it to your prompt"]
    Skip -->|"yes"| Nothing
    Skip -->|"no"| Pipe --> Inject
  end

  Py3 --> Skip

  subgraph Verify["Step 5 -- prove it is actually working, do not assume"]
    direction TB
    Status["hybrid-retrieval status -- file/chunk counts, embedder, ranker metrics. Zero files means the walker excluded everything"]
    Query["hybrid-retrieval query --repo /path/repo 'add jitter to retry backoff' --show-context -- the same pipeline, printed. --local bypasses the daemon entirely, which is how you tell a ranking bug from a stale-daemon bug"]
    Trace["hybrid-retrieval trace --last -- every real hook request writes a row, INCLUDING skipped ones. If the hook is live but silent, the row tells you whether it skipped or gated"]
    Dash["hybrid-retrieval dashboard -- the Pipeline tab runs your prompt through the daemon stage by stage. localhost, no auth"]
    Status --> Query --> Trace --> Dash
  end

  Inject --> Status

  subgraph Fresh["Keeping the index fresh"]
    direction TB
    Watch["The daemon starts a file-watcher on a repo's first prompt, so edits re-index themselves (index/watcher.py, 1s debounce)"]
    Manual["Re-run index after a big rebase or a branch switch that the watcher was not running for"]
    Stale["Changed code the daemon imports? hybrid-retrieval stop FIRST. A resident process holds old modules, and this repo's history is full of 'the fix did not work' that was really a stale daemon"]
  end

  Dash --> Watch --> Manual --> Stale

  Budget["Payload size is the binding constraint, not ranking. Break-even is ~2,095 tokens (bench/breakeven.py). Above ~40KB the harness spills hook output to a file. top_n and max_tokens in .retrieval/config.toml are the dials -- max_tokens is null/uncapped by default. Adding tokens is what loses, not bad ranking"]
  Inject -.-> Budget

  classDef warn fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#b58900
  class Stale,Py3,Budget warn
  classDef must fill:#d4edda,stroke:#28a745
  class Index,Hook must
